{
 "name": "approach to preterm labour overview",
 "width": 1112,
 "title": "Contractions or fluid before 37 weeks: membranes intact with no cervical change is threatened preterm labour (hydrate, treat a urinary infection), with a dilating cervix is preterm labour (tocolysis to buy 48 hours for steroids under 34 weeks and transfer), ruptured membranes is PPROM (confirm, antibiotics, steroids), and an imminent birth adds magnesium sulfate under 34 weeks and penicillin for group B streptococcus; each column gives presentation, numbered investigations and treatment in order",
